      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T15:47:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you really want to clear all bits here?  Doesn\u0027t this introduce race conditions if the PDC generated new connector change events while the PPM is trying to clear the old events?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2446,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2450,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1964e8b8069a9e79db681b0ac29c95581fd17b28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "817d44a7_dd1477e3",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 45
      },
      "lineNbr": 2450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T18:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the spec, *The LPM/PPM shall wait until the OPM Acknowledges the notification (due to an asynchronous event) before sending the next notification.* IIUC, a PDC shall apply the clear bits corresponding to the last CI. If there is another CI, that\u0027s either ignored or stored in a cache for the next notification.\n\nAbhishek?",
      "parentUuid": "657d6859_ba46da3b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2446,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2450,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1964e8b8069a9e79db681b0ac29c95581fd17b28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0e90c56_c5b8ba26",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 45
      },
      "lineNbr": 2450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T22:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should be using the cached `connector_status_change` for the first 16 bits and clearing the latter 16 with 0xffff is fine. There\u0027s also this change coming from PDM: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5535210 which might mean that we can just no-op this command here (I.e. call the command complete right away).\n\nThe better thing to do might be to clear the connector_status_change bits of the cached connector status in `st_read_run` for ACK_CC_CI if we acked any bits (or get rid of the cached state and request re-reading it). You may want to coordinate that with Scott.",
      "parentUuid": "817d44a7_dd1477e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2446,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2450,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1964e8b8069a9e79db681b0ac29c95581fd17b28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fa32674_65c1f988",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 45
      },
      "lineNbr": 2450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T18:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Filed b/343733474. There is a chance that back-to-back CI could be acked by the PPM before the PDM:\n\n1. CI1 arrives.\n1. PDM acks CI1.\n1. CI2 arrives.\n1. PPM intends to ack CI1 but acks CI2.\n1. PDM acks CI2.\n1. PPM acks CI2 (again).\n\nIf PDM or PPM assumes each CI-ACK pair is atomic, the code built on that assumption may break.",
      "parentUuid": "a0e90c56_c5b8ba26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2446,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2450,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "1964e8b8069a9e79db681b0ac29c95581fd17b28",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
